WEBVTT

00:03.840 --> 00:04.160
All right.

00:04.160 --> 00:06.800
So now let's quickly compare the three functions side by side.

00:06.800 --> 00:09.840
Let's start with the first point about the uniqueness of the rank.

00:10.000 --> 00:15.400
And if you compare those three you can see that only the row number generates unique distinct rank.

00:15.560 --> 00:17.600
So this is going to be unique rank.

00:17.600 --> 00:21.760
And the two others we have duplicates or let's say shared ranks okay.

00:21.800 --> 00:26.800
So now the second point whether the function handles the ties and the only one that doesn't handle the

00:26.800 --> 00:28.640
ties is the row number.

00:28.640 --> 00:30.960
So this one doesn't handle the ties.

00:30.960 --> 00:34.960
And the two others handles the ties since they offer the shared rank.

00:35.000 --> 00:39.200
And now we have the last point about leaving gaps or skipping ranking.

00:39.360 --> 00:44.200
So now if you check the row number and the dense rank, you can see there will be no skipping.

00:44.200 --> 00:51.240
So there is no gaps for the row number and as well for the dense rank only for the rank function, the

00:51.240 --> 00:54.680
middle one, we are skipping ranks and we are leaving gaps.

00:54.680 --> 00:55.600
So that's it guys.

00:55.600 --> 00:58.040
This is the differences between those three functions.

00:58.280 --> 01:02.120
I tend usually to work with the row number more often than the two others.
